{"timestamp":"2026-09-23T03:11:23.535Z","ordinal":54,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a0cc3f-1d8f-7c03-9927-47daccb2116a","call_id":"call_gNUsGRGhgTrFTXTbu09H0xi5","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":0,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"c70f2c\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000013376,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1359,\"output\":\"19a15c5 Add hybrid KV storage and pipelined transfers\\n67c4880 Remove PyTorch patch\\n834bb36 Add detailed interval breakdowns\\nf4ab632 Fix pinned host allocator block reuse\\n1005668 Optimize ChunkDelta3 KV decoding\\n331a3d7 Add 4-bit ChunkDelta3 KV compression\\n# CD3 KV hybrid storage\\n\\nCD3 KV defaults to `hybrid` storage and `pipeline` execution. Weight compression\\nand the selected 3-bit/4-bit KV codec are unchanged. Both performance suites\\naccept `--cd3-kv-storage csr|hybrid` and `--cd3-kv-execution serial|pipeline`.\\nThese options affect the CD3 KV-compressed method only.\\n\\n| Comparison | Storage | Execution |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| Original baseline | `csr` | `serial` |\\n| CSR with overlap | `csr` | `pipeline` |\\n| Hybrid without overlap | `hybrid` | `serial` |\\n| Default | `hybrid` | `pipeline` |\\n\\n```bash\\nbash scripts/offline/run_performance_suite.sh \\\\\\n  --methods cao-cd3-fused-kvcomp --batches 64 --repeats 1\\n```\\n\\nUse the same batch list, input/output lengths, KV bits and resource settings\\nwhen comparing runs. The batch list also determines maximum concurrency and\\nHBM KV reservation, so B64 alone and the B64 portion of a B64/B128 run are not\\nidentical A/B conditions. Run without `--breakdown` for performance; enable it\\nonly in separate diagnostics because its synchronization changes execution.\\n\\n## Storage and publication\\n\\nThe encoder writes codes, sign/mantissa, bases and tile offsets directly into\\nthe existing fixed body pool using physical slot IDs. Its Packed20 exception\\nwords and true exception counts use separate worker/chunk scratch rows. The\\nbody is never copied from encoder scratch into a variable-length record.\\n\\nAfter each encoded chunk, a native operation reserves entries space, copies\\nonly the actual words, and creates an immutable pending batch. K/V entries use\\nrequest-owned segments in one shared, bounded arena pool. Whole backing arenas\\nare reserved during warmup; runtime segment allocation uses a native free list\\nand append offsets. It never searches the hugepage allocator's occupied-block\\nlist. There is no Python per-record tensor-view/copy loop.\\n\\nThe main thread publishes only records whose captured slot, generation and\\nimmutable ownership still match. A K or V exception overflow keeps the true\\ncounts, omits the compressed route, and restores both sides from authoritative\\nraw secondary KV. Zero-entry records need no entries segment.\\n\\nThe old maximum-sized entries pool and append-only layer CSR arena are absent\\nin hybrid mode. The original compressed-host allowance is partitioned into\\nfixed bodies, counts, bounded entries scratch, native metadata/workspace, and\\nentries arena capacity. Segment slack and retired reader-held storage consume\\nthat same capacity. Exhaustion raises explicitly; it does not allocate another\\nhidden pool. CSR remains an explicit comparison/fallback path.\\n\\n## Planning, transfer and lifetime\\n\\nOne native record table maps each block generation to its body slot and K/V\\nentry ranges. Planning visits active IDs once, sorts physical body slots once\\nfor both sides, merges adjacent body rows, and gathers exactly the selected\\nentries ranges. Body order and entries storage order can differ; per-row entry\\noffsets connect them. Dead or inactive entries are not transferred as gaps.\\n\\nOne relative plan serves both staging rings. Native submission resolves the\\nselected ring's destination addresses. K body, entries and routing copies are\\nsubmitted together before the K completion event. K restoration can then run\\nwhile V copies proceed; V restoration waits for all V copies. Dense-buffer\\nreuse and the full-KV attention barrier remain unchanged.\\n\\nEntry reader leases retain segments through their final H2D completion.\\nReusable pinned routing snapshots are also returned only after completion.\\nFixed-body writers wait for earlier layer H2D before overwriting a reused slot.\\nConsumed events protect both staging contents and routing through decoder\\nlaunches. Final-reference free does not synchronize CUDA; explicit shutdown\\ndrains work before releasing the store.\\n\\nFull-block-only ownership is required. Legacy partial-block operation uses CSR\\nand reports `requires_full_block_only`. Disabling split loading or using the\\nsame stream reports serial execution. CUDA errors propagate with layer/ring\\ncontext; uncertain source completion retains the affected storage.\\n\\n## Diagnostics\\n\\nOrdinary `kv_metrics.*.csv` records raw-equivalent bytes, compressed payload,\\nactual H2D bytes, K/V bytes, routing metadata, body alignment, gaps, copy\\ndescriptors and batch calls. K includes the common output-ID metadata once.\\nPayload excludes routing metadata and body padding. Raw fallback bytes are\\nincluded in aggregate KV traffic, separately from compressed CD3 counters.\\n\\nOptional CPU diagnostics separate encoding, entries packing/publication,\\nplanning and submission. Native planner counters report visited records,\\nselected entries segments and new reusable backing allocations. Fixed result\\nobjects are not included in the backing-allocation counter. `live_payload_bytes`\\nincludes live fixed bodies and entries; `segment_capacity_bytes` describes only\\nthe entries arenas. `planner_reserved_bytes` is a conservative metadata reserve.\\n\\nThe native planner still rebuilds after membership/record invalidation. It uses\\nbounded reusable workspace and one logical plan for both rings; there is no\\nincremental segment cache or GPU segment indirection in this implementation.\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":1,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"cad37b\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000009344,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1457,\"output\":\"tests/test_cd3_hybrid_storage.py:81:            assert [list(span) for span in snapshot[f\\\"{side}_body_spans\\\"]] == [\\ntests/test_cd3_hybrid_storage.py:85:            words = copied_words(arenas, snapshot[f\\\"{side}_entry_spans\\\"])\\ntests/test_cd3_hybrid_storage.py:116:            spans = snapshot[f\\\"{side}_entry_spans\\\"]\\ntests/test_cd3_hybrid_storage.py:146:            assert snapshot[f\\\"{side}_entry_spans\\\"] == []\\ntiered_serve/chunk_delta3_kv_compressor.py:497:        self._hybrid_planner_bytes = n_layers * _cd3_ext.hybrid_planner_budget(\\ntiered_serve/chunk_delta3_kv_compressor.py:501:            self._encode_chunk_blocks, planner_bytes=self._hybrid_planner_bytes)\\ntiered_serve/chunk_delta3_kv_compressor.py:512:        self._hybrid_planner_bytes += metadata_bytes\\ntiered_serve/chunk_delta3_kv_compressor.py:539:        logger.info(\\\"CD3 hybrid host budget=%d body=%d entries=%d scratch=%d counts=%d planner=%d segment=%d\\\",\\ntiered_serve/chunk_delta3_kv_compressor.py:541:                    budget.count_bytes, self._hybrid_planner_bytes, segment_bytes)\\ntiered_serve/chunk_delta3_kv_compressor.py:1024:            from tiered_serve.chunk_delta3_kv_plan import prepare_hybrid_plan\\ntiered_serve/chunk_delta3_kv_compressor.py:1025:            return prepare_hybrid_plan(self, layer_id, block_ids)\\ntiered_serve/chunk_delta3_kv_compressor.py:1260:            if self.storage_backend != \\\"hybrid\\\" and not plan.native_plans:\\ntiered_serve/chunk_delta3_kv_compressor.py:1336:        hybrid_plan = getattr(plan, \\\"native_plan\\\", None)\\ntiered_serve/chunk_delta3_kv_compressor.py:1337:        native = hybrid_plan if